# --- OpenSSL Configuration (Legacy SQL Server Support) ---
# 
# WHEN TO USE:
# - Ubuntu 22.04 production server connecting to SQL Server 2008/2012
# - You see error: "SSL routines::unsupported protocol"
#
# WHEN NOT NEEDED:
# - Windows development with modern SQL Server (2016+)
# - No SSL/TLS handshake errors
#
# HOW TO SET:
# 1. Ensure the OpenSSL config file exists at the specified path
# 2. The file must have SECLEVEL=0 and UnsafeLegacyRenegotiation=yes
# 3. File must be readable (chmod 644)
#
# Example for Ubuntu production:
# OPENSSL_CONF=/etc/shiny-server/openssl.cnf
#
# Leave commented out for Windows development unless needed:
# OPENSSL_CONF=
